{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works","id":1304088,"title":"Do You Guys Think This Title Works?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-10T20:07:18-07:00","id":1304088,"title":"Do You Guys Think This Title Works?","content":"Ok guys. This will be part love letter,part wish list, and part title suggestion. I've know about Exalted for a while now,but never had ocassion to read its sourcebooks. That changed last month,and since i firmly believe villains hold the story together, after the 2e corebook i've read Manuel to The Infernal and,with the exception of the gross stuff y'all already know about,i've really enjoyed it.<br /> After asking some questions to see what are the plans for the infernals are for this edition. I thought i'd make a thread to discuss what would be the Subtitle for the eventual 3e Infernal book.<br /> How about<br /> <br /> Infernals: A King Never Loses His Majesty<br /> <br /> I thought this subtitle does a subtitle job wonderfully because<br /> A) it sounds incredibly badass<br /> B)it makes poetic sense. The Yozis were once the kings of creation,and now stuck forevermore in Hell,broken and mad. They are still the rightful rulers of everything and their Princes will bring them back.<br /> So,do you guys think such s title works? Is there anything you want to see in the 3e Infernals 2e didnt do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T21:14:30-07:00","id":1304098,"title":"","content":"hm too singular i guess, from how the other subtitles were they were more descriptors of their specific chosen's current affairs and states. &quot;What Fire has Wrought&quot; describes the great civilizations that the DBs have built for themselves in the past millennia, Fangs at the Gate represent the Lunars current tactics, locations, and position in the world alongside their current waves of victory as they are slowly encroaching on the Realm with murderous fury. Rises from the Ashes I think has to do with the symbolic prayer smoke and sacrifice gods have to do to bring forth champions.<br /> <br /> in anywise as for Infernals, I don't think majesty really fits them, they are Solars so its in there but they don't have the same vibe. Rather what these great princes and their chosen have in common is another theme, revenge. In third edition one of the things that the devs are making that it's pretty much an impossibility for a Yozi to escape Malfeas. Or at least it should be impossible(if you want one to escape for a major story plot hook theres no stopping you). because of this most Yozi has given up on returning to Creation, so now they just want to do one thing. To hurt, to wound, to hate on those who trapped them in this Hell, those that betrayed, who harmed them, who killed their brethren and threatened them the same. Infernals are their way how to accomplish that. According to the Devs the condition for the Yozi to choose you now is to have been betrayed by the world and gods, to feel scorn against the ones who attacked you, to wish for revenge. Those are the people who will get Chosen as Infernals now, people the Yozi for as much as they are alien can sympathize. So a title more reflecting on their hate would be more fitting, as it is the now. The idea of kings coming back to their rightful place fits more with the Solars themes(which I think would be nice to have a subtitle also). I would suggest keeping the idea of &quot;kings&quot;(they are still the green sun princes, who as the devs described have giant ziggurat mansions filled with intoxications and pleasure in Malfeas) but instead of keeping a prideful image a avenging one fits more.<br /> <br /> in any case, welcome to Exalted. great that you love the lore and setting, hope you enjoy you stay and keep having fun as the ball gets rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T21:34:13-07:00","id":1304100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304098#post1304098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hm too singular i guess, from how the other subtitles were they were more descriptors of their specific chosen's current affairs and states. &quot;What Fire has Wrought&quot; describes the great civilizations that the DBs have built for themselves in the past millennia, Fangs at the Gate represent the Lunars current tactics, locations, and position in the world alongside their current waves of victory as they are slowly encroaching on the Realm with murderous fury. Rises from the Ashes I think has to do with the symbolic prayer smoke and sacrifice gods have to do to bring forth champions.<br /> <br /> in anywise as for Infernals, I don't think majesty really fits them, they are Solars so its in there but they don't have the same vibe. Rather what these great princes and their chosen have in common is another theme, revenge. In third edition one of the things that the devs are making that it's pretty much an impossibility for a Yozi to escape Malfeas. Or at least it should be impossible(if you want one to escape for a major story plot hook theres no stopping you). because of this most Yozi has given up on returning to Creation, so now they just want to do one thing. To hurt, to wound, to hate on those who trapped them in this Hell, those that betrayed, who harmed them, who killed their brethren and threatened them the same. Infernals are their way how to accomplish that. According to the Devs the condition for the Yozi to choose you now is to have been betrayed by the world and gods, to feel scorn against the ones who attacked you, to wish for revenge. Those are the people who will get Chosen as Infernals now, people the Yozi for as much as they are alien can sympathize. So a title more reflecting on their hate would be more fitting, as it is the now. The idea of kings coming back to their rightful place fits more with the Solars themes(which I think would be nice to have a subtitle also). I would suggest keeping the idea of &quot;kings&quot;(they are still the green sun princes, who as the devs described have giant ziggurat mansions filled with intoxications and pleasure in Malfeas) but instead of keeping a prideful image a avenging one fits more.<br /> <br /> in any case, welcome to Exalted. great that you love the lore and setting, hope you enjoy you stay and keep having fun as the ball gets rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thank you for the welcome<br /> i'll keept thinking on different tiles based on what you said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:35:29-07:00","id":1304162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works#post1304088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernals: A King Never Loses His Majesty</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this is a bit too much of a mouthful for a title in its own right, and especially when existing Exalted sourcebooks have established a nice pattern for short, punchy titles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything you want to see in the 3e Infernals 2e didnt do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually talking about the experience and likely motivations of its Exalted would be nice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:17:29-07:00","id":1304216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304162#post1304162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though this is a bit too much of a mouthful for a title in its own right, and especially when existing Exalted sourcebooks have established a nice pattern for short, punchy titles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually talking about the experience and likely motivations of its Exalted would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its a good bet this edition will have that,i'm excites for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:04:59-07:00","id":1304225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually talking about the experience and likely motivations of its Exalted would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, that's true. It did often seem like the fluff was &quot;The Yozis plans, and their servants who'll carry it out.&quot; And the motivation for the Infernals mostly seemed to be &quot;The Yozis will give you stuff. But also screw with you.&quot; Which wasn't utterly compelling.<br /> I guess it was a slightly similar issue to Abyssals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is there anything you want to see in the 3e Infernals 2e didnt do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe a slightly more unified theme would help. I really liked reading Infernals, but when we actually did a game they felt like each character was 1-2 different themes stuck together. Ie you didn't feel like a Demonic exalt, but like a half-Shadow, half-Wind Exalt, or a Sand-and-telekinesis exalt. Some characters were better than others. (My friend played a green fire/wish-granting exalt, which did feel more like a Demonic exalt than the others.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernals: A King Never Loses His Majesty</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with Isator here. I like the idea behind it, but it's a bit long. &quot;Lunars: Fangs at the Gate&quot; has 5 words, as does &quot;Dragonblood: What Fire has Wrought&quot;, whereas that has 7.<br /> <br /> But I do like yur idea of doing something related to Kings, such as words like &quot;Kings&quot;, &quot;Majesty&quot;, &quot;Princes&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> Like:<br /> Infernals: To Rule in Hell<br /> Infernals: Princes of Blasphemy<br /> Something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-11-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:44:12-07:00","id":1304245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304225#post1304225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, that's true. It did often seem like the fluff was &quot;The Yozis plans, and their servants who'll carry it out.&quot; And the motivation for the Infernals mostly seemed to be &quot;The Yozis will give you stuff. But also screw with you.&quot; Which wasn't utterly compelling.<br /> I guess it was a slightly similar issue to Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time around when I could only post to this forum via my phone, I considered starting a thread laying out my thoughts on the game's historical issues with presenting what could be crudely described as the &quot;villain Exalted&quot;. The game never quite seemed to want to commit to the old World of Darkness approach of leaning into that (which I think would have been the wrong call anyway), but they never really seem to me to have had much thought for what the alternative was.<br /> <br /> I do think that the Yozis and Deathlords do have a place in the stories of those Exalted, but I think they need to take a few steps back; they wine and dine their new Chosen, they present an ethos (which still needs to be a bit more sophisticated and focused on the Exalted themselves), and the rest is then about what these people are liable to do with their new positions.<br /> <br /> I do have hopes, though; the focus on Abyssals as Death's Lawgivers and the chivalry they carry, and reconceptualising the Reclamation as the premise of Infernals acquiring control of Creation that their Essences remember.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:47:23-07:00","id":1304247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304225#post1304225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, that's true. It did often seem like the fluff was &quot;The Yozis plans, and their servants who'll carry it out.&quot; And the motivation for the Infernals mostly seemed to be &quot;The Yozis will give you stuff. But also screw with you.&quot; Which wasn't utterly compelling.<br /> I guess it was a slightly similar issue to Abyssals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think maybe a slightly more unified theme would help. I really liked reading Infernals, but when we actually did a game they felt like each character was 1-2 different themes stuck together. Ie you didn't feel like a Demonic exalt, but like a half-Shadow, half-Wind Exalt, or a Sand-and-telekinesis exalt. Some characters were better than others. (My friend played a green fire/wish-granting exalt, which did feel more like a Demonic exalt than the others.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I kind of agree with Isator here. I like the idea behind it, but it's a bit long. &quot;Lunars: Fangs at the Gate&quot; has 5 words, as does &quot;Dragonblood: What Fire has Wrought&quot;, whereas that has 7.<br /> <br /> But I do like yur idea of doing something related to Kings, such as words like &quot;Kings&quot;, &quot;Majesty&quot;, &quot;Princes&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> Like:<br /> Infernals: To Rule in Hell<br /> Infernals: Princes of Blasphemy<br /> Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>i be Liking your ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T20:39:57-07:00","id":1304385,"title":"","content":"Infernals: At first you Can't Succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T22:00:46-07:00","id":1304396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304225#post1304225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like:<br /> Infernals: To Rule in Hell<br /> Infernals: Princes of Blasphemy<br /> Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, Infernals: To Rule in Hell is the name of Lenaya\u00b4s Third Edition version of them. And both the name and the conversion are awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T01:38:47-07:00","id":1304413,"title":"","content":"Actually, To Reign in Hell would be better.<br /> <br /> Of course, you actually want to reign in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T02:02:38-07:00","id":1304416,"title":"","content":"Vance talked about Infernals as having the choice between razing Creation or turning it into paradise (under their rule), which lead me to the title &quot;Infernals: To Bless or Burn&quot;<br /> <br /> Some other title ideas:<br /> Infernals: Deal with the Devil<br /> Infernals: The Thrones of Hell<br /> Infernals: Under a Hellfire Sun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T04:56:29-07:00","id":1304429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KuiperBelt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304088-do-you-guys-think-this-title-works?p=1304416#post1304416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance talked about Infernals as having the choice between razing Creation or turning it into paradise (under their rule), which lead me to the title &amp;quot;Infernals: To Bless or Burn&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Some other title ideas:<br /> Infernals: Deal with the Devil<br /> Infernals: The Thrones of Hell<br /> Infernals: Under a Hellfire Sun</div> </div> </div> </div>Hellfire Sun is my favorite so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:29:48-07:00","id":1304471,"title":"","content":"Oh,i just thought of new,shorter one.<br /> <br /> Infernals: Primeval Mythos.<br /> <br /> This is one is based on how ancient the Yozis are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}